<HEAD><style>.gml-card { --rule: var(--neutral-border-color); --leaf-ink: var(--palette-eucalyptus, var(--palette-2)); --mist-field: var(--palette-mist, var(--palette-4)); }
.photo-reading-panel { background-color: var(--surface-color); border-left: 3pt solid var(--leaf-ink); padding: 22pt 24pt 20pt; box-sizing: border-box; }
.gml-card { background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 22% 18%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-color) 22%, transparent) 0 1pt, transparent 1.4pt); background-size: 15pt 15pt; }
.gml-grid-cell { --cell-radius: 0; }
.botanical-rule { --divider-color: var(--leaf-ink); --divider-thickness: 1pt; }
.botanical-rule.gml-divider { opacity: .72; }
.line-botanical .gml-icon { opacity: .62; }
.care-columns .gml-icon { width: 34pt; height: 34pt; font-size: 24pt; }
.care-list, .comparison-ledger { margin-block-start: var(--heading-gap-above); }
.alt-paths { --marker-font-size: calc(11 * var(--type-anchor, 1pt)); --marker-font-weight: 600; --marker-color: var(--body-color-muted); }
.alt-paths .gml-grid-cell__marker { letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.botanical-badges .gml-icon { width: 58pt; height: 58pt; font-size: 30pt; padding: 11pt; box-sizing: border-box; border: 1pt solid var(--leaf-ink); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--leaf-ink); opacity: .82; }
.ripple-field.gml-grid-cell { background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 70% 56%, transparent 0 18%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--leaf-ink) 45%, transparent) 18.3% 18.7%, transparent 19% 28%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--leaf-ink) 32%, transparent) 28.3% 28.7%, transparent 29%); }
.gml-table { --table-border-color: var(--rule); --table-border-width: 1pt; --table-header-bg: var(--mist-field); --table-header-color: var(--heading-color); --table-header-weight: 600; --table-stripe-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mist-field) 38%, transparent); --table-cell-padding-block: 9pt; --table-cell-padding-inline: 12pt; --table-radius: 0; }
.gml-chart { --gamma-chart-grid-color: var(--neutral-border-color); --gamma-chart-axis-color: var(--body-color-muted); --gamma-chart-text-color: var(--body-color); --gamma-chart-bar-radius: 1pt; }
.gml-card__footer { color: var(--body-color-muted); letter-spacing: .08em; }</style></HEAD>
<section image-layout="blank" id="eWxhtwT8f9" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="K092nu-yvZ" padding="0" rowspan="42"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="Do0-0Rv1m5" background-color="palette-4" vertical-align="end" padding="48pt 54pt" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">The Restorative Hour</p><display size="md" font-size="54pt">A better stay can begin in one hour</display><h3 role="subheading">A guided in-property ritual that helps guests shift from travel mode into the character and pace of the hotel.</h3></grid-item><grid-item id="aTC-xUr8ap" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/ECudr8PsVVU7NLiqfZDXT.png" saved-media-id="lihsuystxlagr9d" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="winter-glasshouse" alt="Soft editorial photograph of a quiet boutique-hotel room prepared for a small guided restorative session, eight simple movable seats arranged with generous space, a water station and folded approved materials on a side surface, diffuse winter daylight, warm ivory and layered sage-green palette, tactile architectural finishes, airy negative space, low contrast, matte finish, absolutely no people, body parts, reflections, logos, signage, or text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1440,&quot;height&quot;:1440}"></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="xed2AcbodP" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="28pt 54pt" rowspan="18"><grid divider="sm neutral-border"><grid-item id="fB8zGN8K-D" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Guest promise</p><h3>One calm, considered moment built into the stay.</h3></grid-item><grid-item id="eJjYVxRN5z" colspan="30"><p role="eyebrow">Manager proposition</p><h3>A distinctive experience with a defined format, operating model, and pilot decision.</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="HtfVUgZLge" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sHtgrFH4RF" padding="44pt 54pt 40pt"><p role="eyebrow">The guest journey</p><h1>The stay has a missing middle</h1><p font-size="16pt">The overlooked opportunity sits between arriving at the property and feeling present within it.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><smart-layout variant="minimalTimelineWithBoxes" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Arrive</h4><p>Bags, logistics, notifications, and unfamiliar surroundings compete for attention.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Reset</h4><p>A hosted ritual creates a clear pause and introduces the hotel’s way of caring.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Return</h4><p>The guest continues with an experience to describe, repeat, or add to a future booking.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="H-etSNxZRG" background-color="palette-4" padding="14pt 18pt"><p><b>This is hospitality wellness, not a medical intervention.</b> The value begins with thoughtful time, place, and attention.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="cD-enucdgc" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="d_0vXlaN7d" padding="38pt 48pt 40pt"><p role="eyebrow">A consistent spine · property-specific character</p><h1>The 60-minute guest ritual</h1><p>A repeatable sequence creates operational discipline; the setting and chosen practice make it belong to the hotel.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="3goCTJyCVq" colspan="12"><p role="eyebrow">0–5 minutes</p><h3>Welcome</h3><p font-size="12.5pt">Greet personally, orient the guest, and offer a simple choice of pace or position.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5hx6Hpma0U" colspan="12"><p role="eyebrow">5–15 minutes</p><h3>Arrive</h3><p font-size="12.5pt">Use accessible breath, mobility, or sensory grounding within the practitioner’s qualifications.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="uIrcWSeB6U" background-color="palette-4" colspan="12"><p role="eyebrow">15–40 minutes</p><h3>Restore</h3><p font-size="12.5pt">Guide stretching, sound, quiet movement, or seated relaxation.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="b4Eh9REUpb" colspan="12"><p role="eyebrow">40–55 minutes</p><h3>Linger</h3><p font-size="12.5pt">Offer tea, water, journaling, or silence connected to the place and time of day.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="5DfLsSFedz" colspan="12"><p role="eyebrow">55–60 minutes</p><h3>Close</h3><p font-size="12.5pt">Mark a clear ending, offer an optional takeaway, and return the guest warmly to the stay.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="6PN3TXlEYB" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="H4_VoqE-W8" padding="42pt 52pt 38pt"><p role="eyebrow">A proposition to validate</p><h1>One hour creates three kinds of value</h1><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug" class="line-botanical care-columns"><grid-item id="3tqdsulOco" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/67bzhWQWPYkFDPeA4ccyXv.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="hotel guest arrival key" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black key on a white background, embodying the concept of state-key, a crucial element for security and access control.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>For guests</h3><p>A low-friction way to pause without arranging an off-property appointment or committing to a clinical treatment.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NFmu1KZsD6" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/Hz8dji8ViGQtRpEaaRXyph.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="hotel staff booking handoff" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black shape of a building with a triangular roof, symbolizing accommodation and hospitality, embodying the concept of a hotel.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>For staff</h3><p>A defined offer, booking script, capacity limit, and practitioner handoff reduce ambiguity about what is sold and who delivers it.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3RMCihza4o" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="20"><grid-item-label><icon src="https://iconscdn.pictographic.ai/image/A5jwCohoqbghd0H82K82.svg?stroke=45" source="image.pictographic.icon" alt="boutique hotel distinctive experience" meta="{&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A black void or emptiness in a white space, signifying the concept of experience as a blank slate or a foundation for knowledge and events to unfold.&quot;}"></icon></grid-item-label><h3>For the property</h3><p>Differentiation, an ancillary charge or package allocation, and a guest story that expresses the hotel’s character.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><hr color="palette-2" thickness="sm" class="botanical-rule"><p role="eyebrow">The relationship to test</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="Q25NoPirRE" colspan="15"><h4>Guest interest</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="lcfHDe56i0" colspan="15"><h4>Bookings</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="A0ugyYgtjQ" colspan="15"><h4>Manageable operation</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="xnFYUdZ_LY" colspan="15"><h4>Positive contribution</h4></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">The pilot measures each link rather than assuming it.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="0RCUEbm9QA" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1r7dOcpzwk" background-color="palette-4" padding="42pt 34pt 38pt 48pt" colspan="19"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative operating model</p><h1 font-size="34pt">Hospitality onstage; choreography backstage</h1><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><display size="md" font-size="48pt">2</display><p role="caption">60-minute sessions per day</p><hr color="palette-2" width="sm" class="botanical-rule"><display size="md" font-size="48pt">8</display><p role="caption">Guest places per session</p><hr color="palette-2" width="sm" class="botanical-rule"><display size="md" font-size="48pt">15</display><p role="caption">Minute room turn after each session</p></grid-item><grid-item id="4GKiXB8BFx" padding="38pt 50pt 34pt 34pt" colspan="41"><p role="eyebrow">One controlled inventory · one suitable flexible room</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 28pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="AC0RTmUXRO" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Offer</h4><p font-size="12.5pt">Reservations or front desk present the ritual before arrival, at check-in, or in-stay; availability comes from one inventory.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="X9lML5-4TA" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Prepare</h4><p font-size="12.5pt">The hotel host checks the room, accessible route, water, linens, seating, temperature, and approved materials.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="p-weVctvuS" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Deliver</h4><p font-size="12.5pt">A qualified practitioner owns the practice and safety boundaries; the host owns the welcome and guest handoff.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="bdQPdSXzRA" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Reset</h4><p font-size="12.5pt">Restore the room to a documented standard before the next session.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="vSMHjDDxcB" padding="10pt 0"><h4>Learn</h4><p font-size="12.5pt">Record attendance, anonymous feedback, staff handling time, and direct costs—without unnecessary health information.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="qjJsJZllAx" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="jG0n60vYFV" padding="36pt 50pt 30pt"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative example — not actual company or hotel performance</p><h1>A scenario managers can replace with property data</h1><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="gkLvloxh2w" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><graph chart-type="column" show-data-labels="true" effect="none" chart-font="body" text-size="md" width="500pt" height="245pt"><properties><property key="fill" label="Seat fill" type="label"></property><property key="contribution" label="Monthly contribution (USD)" type="data"></property></properties><data><row><cell>35% fill</cell><cell>-100</cell></row><row><cell>50% fill</cell><cell>3500</cell></row><row><cell>65% fill</cell><cell>7100</cell></row></data></graph><p role="caption">Sensitivity under the illustrative assumptions.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IRpmmimlL7" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" padding="18pt 20pt" colspan="22"><p role="eyebrow">Base case · 50% fill</p><display size="md" font-size="52pt">$3,500</display><p role="caption">Illustrative monthly contribution</p><table col-widths="[38,62]" borders="rows" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p><b>Capacity</b></p></td><td><p>2 × 8 × 30 = 480 places</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Revenue</b></p></td><td><p>240 × $55 = $13,200</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Practitioner</b></p></td><td><p>60 × $125 = $7,500</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Consumables</b></p></td><td><p>240 × $5 = $1,200</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><b>Support</b></p></td><td><p>$1,000 fixed</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>$13,200 − $7,500 − $1,200 − $1,000 = $3,500.</b></p><p role="caption">Break-even ≈ 170 participants · 36% seat fill.</p></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Contribution excludes internal hotel labor, room opportunity cost, taxes, payment fees, and capital expenditure.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="JBnZ6P6ztr" vertical-align="start"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="CffTzexGAZ" padding="38pt 50pt 34pt"><p role="eyebrow">Six-week pilot structure</p><h1>Prove the experience before scaling it</h1><smart-layout variant="minimalTimelineWithBoxes" orientation="horizontal" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>Weeks 1–2 · Prepare</h4><p>Select the ritual and room; confirm credentials, local requirements, guest script, and booking handoff.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Weeks 3–6 · Operate</h4><p>Run the agreed calendar, review attendance and issues weekly, and collect one short rating plus optional comments.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>End of week 6 · Decide</h4><p>Continue, adapt, or stop according to evidence from guests, staff, and the commercial model.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative decision gates · agree with the property</p><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="g0iZy2Mx4B" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h3>≥ 40%</h3><p role="caption">Seat fill</p></grid-item><grid-item id="hevdAQTZN2" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h3>≤ 15%</h3><p role="caption">No-show rate</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ksco3ZReUB" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h3>≥ 4.5 / 5</h3><p role="caption">Average guest rating</p></grid-item><grid-item id="UEEoBY4n9D" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>No unresolved issues</h4><p role="caption">Safety or service</p></grid-item><grid-item id="xPU3IUIumk" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>Within the limit</h4><p role="caption">Incremental administration</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZlEDp1p9hy" cell-style="subtle" padding="10pt 14pt" colspan="20"><h4>Positive contribution</h4><p role="caption">After agreed direct costs</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="QNZI6DzMc7" vertical-align="start" card-margin-hidden="true"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="eCAnlOIriZ" padding="0" rowspan="12"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/Np-k3WrU4cQHYeIFa16zb.png" saved-media-id="wnl1f2v6dmwr6g5" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="winter-glasshouse" alt="Soft documentary photograph of a flexible boutique-hotel room ready to host a small restorative hour, movable seating aligned beside an open floor area, water and a simple preparation checklist without legible text on a work surface, diffuse winter daylight across warm ivory walls and sage-green architectural details, airy negative space, low contrast, matte finish, absolutely no people, body parts, reflections, logos, signage, or readable text" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1920,&quot;height&quot;:1088}"></grid-item><grid-item id="AIlS2lUoR0" vertical-align="end" padding="38pt 56pt 34pt" rowspan="48"><p role="eyebrow">The next decision</p><h1>Make room for a restorative hour</h1><p font-size="16pt"><b>The proposal is not to build a spa. It is to test one memorable, well-run hour that belongs to this property.</b></p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="PnOTmVRl_Y" colspan="20"><h3>Name an owner</h3><p>Appoint one property sponsor for guest experience, operations, and the pilot decision.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="fps6wv_X51" colspan="20"><h3>Name the room and rhythm</h3><p>Identify a suitable flexible space and the session times that fit the stay.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="b_3fMCxxd4" colspan="20"><h3>Agree the evidence</h3><p>Replace the illustrative assumptions with property costs, pricing, capacity, and success gates.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><p role="caption">The next working session should leave the team with a chosen ritual, accountable roles, a costed scenario, and a clear go-or-no-go pilot decision.</p></grid-item></grid></section>